content.text:
Now CSS. Add around dialogue styles:
```css
.dialogue-voice { display:inline-flex; align-items:center; gap:2px; margin-left:auto; margin-right:8px; height:9px; opacity:.25; transition:opacity .2s; }
.dialogue-voice em { font-style:normal; font-size:5px; letter-spacing:.12em; color: var(--teal); margin-left:2px; }
.dialogue-voice i { width:2px; height:4px; border-radius:1px; background:var(--teal); transform-origin:bottom; }
.dialogue-voice.speaking { opacity:1; }
.dialogue-voice.speaking i { animation: voiceBar .55s ease-in-out infinite alternate; }
... nth delays
.dialogue-voice.off { opacity:.12; }
@keyframes voiceBar { to { transform: scaleY(2.6); } }
```
But `.dialogue-top span` font-size 6px applies to indicator; `em` font-size 5px okay. `.dialogue-voice` margin-left:auto pushes lang to right; top currently justify-content: space-between, with 3 children. If margin-left:auto, name left, indicator right plus lang. Fine. Better `gap: 10px` maybe. Use `margin-left:auto`.
- For indicator width: em "IA".
- `#dialogue-lang` existing style.

Settings voice CSS:
```css
.voice-status { color: var(--teal) !important; font-size:5.5px !important; letter-spacing:.04em; text-transform:none; display:block; max-width:220px; line-height:1.3; }
.voice-status.fallback { color: var(--gold) !important; }
.voice-test-group { gap:5px !important; }
.voice-test { padding:4px 6px; border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.12); background:rgba(255,255,255,.04); color:var(--muted); font-size:6px; letter-spacing:.06em; border-radius:2px; }
.voice-test:hover, .voice-test.playing { color:#171005; background:var(--gold); border-color:var(--gold); }
```
Need `.setting-label small` style? existing maybe. Search.

