content.text:
The layout now:
- Stick base 96 (looks good).
- D-pad 100 at x140, right of stick; labels visible (CEL/ARMA/RÁDIO/MAPA) but RÁDIO/MAPA bottom clipped? Looks complete.
- Face buttons 48*.98=47; good size. Diamond correctly oriented.
- Ammo card at top-right overlaps the "wanted" area? It shows at y~100-ish "GENERAL... 09/48(?)". Wait, there's a card at top right showing "GENERAL" or "PISTOLA" and "09 / 48" — that's the weapon card. It overlaps some scene, fine. It reads "GENERAL"? Actually it's the weapon card with icon and text; blurred due to screenshot.
- L2/R2 triggers are visible at y~150; labels MIRA and ATIRAR. Good.
- L1/R1 at y~185; labels ARMA and RECARGA (readable).
- R3 center tiny; looks like a small "R3" dot. Fine.
- Objective card and interaction prompt at bottom center: "ENTRAR" prompt now appears (near the truck). It overlaps the cross button? No.
- **Problem**: the bottom-right face buttons overlap the weapon/ammo HUD? No, ammo moved top.
- **Problem**: the D-pad's "RÁDIO" and "MAPA" labels are clipped at the bottom edge? In screenshot, the dpad bottom at y~382, labels at bottom edge; the "MOVER" caption below stick is at y~385 nearly cut. The viewport height 390; safe. The game canvas ends at 390; labels at 377. Fine.
- The mission objective card is hidden? In this screenshot, it's not shown (maybe mission complete / free roam no objective), but the interaction prompt "ENTRAR" shows center. Fine.

The top system bar labels are visible: CREATE TOUCHPAD CELULAR TROCAR OPTIONS. Nice.

Ammo card top-right is cut off? It extends beyond the right edge? It looks like it's clipped at x=844 (the weapon card right 14 + scale .92, should fit). The card in screenshot spans x~700..830, so fits. However its top at 104 is below the money at ~60; good. But the "RECARGA" reload button inside the weapon card might be tiny; irrelevant.

Potential issue: `#bottom-right` also contains the desktop control hints, hidden on touch. Good.

Another issue: the **top system bar** overlaps the **look-zone** but is above; good.

Now, the look/feel is much better. To make it "mais melhor" further:
- Add a subtle PS5-style label/hint when pressing L2 aim: crosshair already changes.
- Add active state for aim (L2 toggle) — currently `held` class removed immediately on release, so no persistent indication that aiming is on. Add `.on` class to L2 when aiming, synced in `setAiming`. Good UX: L2 stays gold outlined while aim mode active.
- Similarly L3 `.on` persists (works).
- Add active state for fire? held while pressed (works).
- For touch attack circle: tap fires, no persistent.
- Add pressed state for D-pad/others via `.held` (works).
- Add an **auto-aim assist**? Maybe not.
- Add a **sprint state indication** on screen? L3 on is gold.
- Add **PS5 haptics patterns**: haptic on fire? fire() currently calls navigator.vibrate maybe on hit only. Add small haptic on shoot (settings.haptics) — but every shot vibration could be heavy; on mobile, short 8ms. Could add in fire() `this.haptic(6)`; but 10 shots/sec of vibration is bad. Skip.
- Add **double-tap stick to sprint**? Not needed with L3.
- Add **L3 hold horn**? currently tap.
- Add **R1 long press**? no.

More "complete" ideas:
- The top system bar's "CREATE" screenshot: does it work in headless? We can test `game.captureScreenshot()`; Chromium may download and playwright might block. We can call and check no error/toast. Later.
- Character switch button works.
- Options opens pause; tested via old mobile-pause? Not yet; test.
- Touchpad opens map; tested via dpad map.
- Phone opens; tested.
- The radio toggle: D-pad right always next station; no off. Maybe long-press toggles. Let's add long-press (500ms) to radio: tap next, hold toggle. This adds completeness.
- Maybe use a "hold" on L1 to open weapon wheel? Too much.

Also **legend/help overlay**: The controls tab documents them, good.

Fix `aim` persistent class:
- In `setAiming`, toggle `.on` on `#touch-l2`.
- CSS `.ps-trigger.on` similar to held but persistent gold.
- When entering vehicle, touchBrake on L2 should be `.held`, and remove `.on`? `setAiming` isn't called on entering vehicle; if aiming was on before entering, `updateTouchContext` doesn't clear `aiming`. Should clear aiming when entering a vehicle (GTA does). Add `this.setAiming(false)` in enterVehicle. Then L2 label FREIO and no gold.
- On exiting, aim stays false.
- In `setAiming`, if no element, fine.
- For desktop right-click, the touch L2 also lights gold (nice, consistent).

Ammo card: maybe add ammo count to the R2 trigger label? e.g., R2 small shows "ATIRAR · 28". But updating every shot could be done in UI update; already `#ammo` exists. The card is visible top-right, acceptable.

**Position of ammo card**: at top 104 it might overlap the mission objective on portrait? We set portrait top 152. In landscape it's good. But on devices with notches, safe-top handled.

**Left-handed layout test**: set settings.hudLayout left via UI or body.lefty; check mirror. Use run-code to add class lefty and screenshot. Also the dpad in lefty is right of stick? CSS `right:150px` and stick right 24, so dpad is left of stick; good. Weapon card left 14. Look zone left top 34%. System bar center. Test.

**Landscape narrow 667x375**: check overlaps. Use viewport resize and body.touch. Screenshot. 

**Portrait 390x844**: check layout; body.touch, media portrait. The game is landscape-oriented but ensure controls don't collide. Screenshot.

Let's implement L2 on state and radio long-press first.

Radio long-press:
In bindTouch handler, currently action `radio` calls `this.nextRadio()` on pointerdown. Change to:
- special-case in pointerdown: for action 'radio', start a timer 550ms; if timer fires, `this.toggleRadio()`, set `longFired=true`, add `held`; on release, if !longFired → nextRadio.
Need local vars per button closure:
```js
let longTimer = null, longFired = false;
```
In release: clear timer; if action==='radio' && !longFired → this.nextRadio(); (but release currently also clears held state)
In pointerdown for radio: don't switch immediately; set longFired=false; longTimer=setTimeout(...); return? But we still want held state/haptic. Add case 'radio': schedule and break. On pointerup release handles tap.
But `pointercancel` should clear and not trigger nextRadio. release currently generic; differentiate cancel vs up? Simpler: on pointerup always trigger tap if !longFired; on pointercancel do not. Current `release` used for both. Split:
```js
const cancel = () => { clearTimeout(longTimer); btn.classList.remove('held'); ... };
const up = () => { ...; if (action==='radio' && !longFired) this.nextRadio(); };
```
Refactor handler. Also `lostpointercapture` fires after pointerup; it would call up twice → radio next twice. Need guard flag `pressed`. Set `pressed=true` on pointerdown, in up/cancel check `if(!pressed)return; pressed=false;`. For synthetic test, pointerup then lostpointercapture → guard.

Let's rewrite the button handler section via Python replacement.

Current block:
```js
    document.querySelectorAll('[data-action]').forEach(btn => {
      if (!btn.closest('.mobile-controls')) return;
      const action = btn.dataset.action;
      const hold = btn.dataset.hold === 'true';
      const release = () => {
        btn.classList.remove('held');
        if (action === 'fire') this.touchFireHeld = false;
        if (action === 'aim') this.touchBrake = false;
      };
      btn.addEventListener('pointerdown', (e) => {
        ...
        switch (action) {
          ...
          case 'radio':
            this.nextRadio();
            break;
        }
      });
      btn.addEventListener('pointerup', release);
      btn.addEventListener('pointercancel', release);
      btn.addEventListener('lostpointercapture', release);
    });
```

Replace with pressed/long logic. Use action radio only. Also for `hold` aim brake release.

New:
```js
    document.querySelectorAll('[data-action]').forEach(btn => {
      if (!btn.closest('.mobile-controls')) return;
      const action = btn.dataset.action;
      const hold = btn.dataset.hold === 'true';
      let pressed = false, longTimer = null, longFired = false;
      const stopHold = () => {
        btn.classList.remove('held');
        if (action === 'fire') this.touchFireHeld = false;
        if (action === 'aim') this.touchBrake = false;
        if (longTimer) { clearTimeout(longTimer); longTimer = null; }
      };
      const up = () => {
        if (!pressed) return;
        pressed = false;
        const wasLong = longFired; longFired = false;
        stopHold();
        if (action === 'radio' && !wasLong) this.nextRadio();
      };
      const cancel = () => {
        if (!pressed) return;
        pressed = false; longFired = false;
        stopHold();
      };
      btn.addEventListener('pointerdown', (e) => {
        ...
        pressed = true;
        btn.classList.add('held');
        ...
        switch (action) {
          ...
          case 'radio':
            longFired = false;
            longTimer = setTimeout(() => {
              longFired = true;
              btn.classList.remove('held');
              this.toggleRadio();
            }, 550);
            break;
        }
      });
      btn.addEventListener('pointerup', up);
      btn.addEventListener('pointercancel', cancel);
      btn.addEventListener('lostpointercapture', cancel); // but after up, pressed false so ignored
    });
```
Careful: `lostpointercapture` fires after `pointerup` normally; `up` sets pressed=false, then cancel sees pressed false → return. Good. But in some browsers lostpointercapture may fire before pointerup? Then cancel clears and radio tap lost. Hmm. Usually pointerup then lost capture. Acceptable. Could not listen to lostpointercapture for buttons and rely on pointercancel; pointer capture ensures pointerup. Keep lostpointercapture but add a small delay? Simpler: remove lostpointercapture listener for buttons; pointerup/cancel are enough with capture. On browsers that lose capture unexpectedly, held state could stick. But `pointercancel` fires. Let's keep lostpointercapture only for `touchFireHeld` safety: in cancel, if fire clear. If lost capture before up, radio tap lost, minor.

Actually to avoid duplicate/lost issues, don't call `stopHold` in `up` before checking? fine.

Now aim `.on`:
```js
  setAiming(on) {
    this.aiming = !!on;
    ...
    const aimBtn = document.querySelector('#touch-l2');
    if (aimBtn) aimBtn.classList.toggle('on', this.aiming && !this.inVehicle);
  }
```
CSS add `.ps-trigger.on` with teal or gold. Gold might conflict with label; use teal (`--teal`) for aim mode. PS5 adaptive trigger vibe: use gold. We'll use gold with a dot.

EnterVehicle: `this.setAiming(false);` (updates L2).
ExitVehicle no.

Also updateTouchContext sets label but if aiming and entering, class removed by setAiming.

Let's patch.

input.command:
python3 - <<'PY'
p='src/main.js'
s=open(p).read()
old_sig="""  setAiming(on) {
    this.aiming = !!on;
    const crosshair = document.querySelector('#crosshair');
    if (crosshair) crosshair.classList.toggle('aiming', this.aiming);
  }"""
new_sig="""  setAiming(on) {
    this.aiming = !!on;
    const crosshair = document.querySelector('#crosshair');
    if (crosshair) crosshair.classList.toggle('aiming', this.aiming);
    const aimBtn = document.querySelector('#touch-l2');
    if (aimBtn) aimBtn.classList.toggle('on', this.aiming && !this.inVehicle);
  }"""
assert old_sig in s
s=s.replace(old_sig,new_sig)
old_handler=s[s.index("    document.querySelectorAll('[data-action]').forEach(btn => {"):s.index("    const l3 = document.querySelector('#touch-l3');")]
new_handler="""    document.querySelectorAll('[data-action]').forEach(btn => {
      if (!btn.closest('.mobile-controls')) return;
      const action = btn.dataset.action;
      const hold = btn.dataset.hold === 'true';
      let pressed = false, longTimer = null, longFired = false;
      const stopHold = () => {
        btn.classList.remove('held');
        if (action === 'fire') this.touchFireHeld = false;
        if (action === 'aim') this.touchBrake = false;
        if (longTimer) { clearTimeout(longTimer); longTimer = null; }
      };
      const release = () => {
        if (!pressed) return;
        pressed = false;
        const wasLong = longFired;
        longFired = false;
        stopHold();
        if (action === 'radio' && !wasLong) this.nextRadio();
      };
      const cancel = () => {
        if (!pressed) return;
        pressed = false;
        longFired = false;
        stopHold();
      };
      btn.addEventListener('pointerdown', (e) => {
        e.preventDefault();
        e.stopPropagation();
        this.audio.init();
        this.audio.resume?.();
        if (this.state !== 'playing') return;
        pressed = true;
        try { btn.setPointerCapture?.(e.pointerId); } catch { /* synthetic pointer */ }
        btn.classList.add('held');
        this.haptic(8);
        switch (action) {
          case 'interact':
            this.interact();
            break;
          case 'fire':
            if (this.inVehicle) this.audio.horn?.();
            else if (hold) { this.touchFireHeld = true; this.fire(); }
            else this.fire();
            break;
          case 'jump':
            this.jumpRequested = true;
            break;
          case 'vehicle':
            this.toggleVehicle();
            break;
          case 'switch':
            this.switchCharacter();
            break;
          case 'reload':
            if (this.inVehicle) this.nextRadio();
            else this.reload();
            break;
          case 'weapon':
            this.switchWeapon();
            break;
          case 'aim':
            if (this.inVehicle) this.touchBrake = true;
            else this.setAiming(!this.aiming);
            break;
          case 'camera':
            this.centerCamera();
            break;
          case 'phone':
            this.ui.openPhone();
            break;
          case 'map':
            this.ui.openMap();
            break;
          case 'radio':
            longFired = false;
            longTimer = setTimeout(() => {
              longFired = true;
              btn.classList.remove('held');
              this.toggleRadio();
            }, 550);
            break;
        }
      });
      btn.addEventListener('pointerup', release);
      btn.addEventListener('pointercancel', cancel);
      btn.addEventListener('lostpointercapture', cancel);
    });

"""
s=s.replace(old_handler,new_handler)
# clear aim when entering vehicle
s=s.replace("""    this.inVehicle = true;
    this.touchSprint = false;
    this.touchBrake = false;
    this.touchFireHeld = false;""","""    this.inVehicle = true;
    this.touchSprint = false;
    this.touchBrake = false;
    this.touchFireHeld = false;
    this.setAiming(false);""")
open(p,'w').write(s)
print('patched')
